RK628F backport for Aiden SCH v1
==============================

Source: https://github.com/rockchip-linux/kernel
Branch: develop-5.10
Commit: 81417fbf13edb25f203ea794a723b8bf1f457d5c
Directory: drivers/media/i2c/rk628
Dependency: include/uapi/linux/rk_hdmirx_config.h

The original BSP driver only implements RK628D. Aiden silicon reports
0x20230321 at GRF_SOC_VERSION (0x0200), identifying RK628F. Backport the
coherent receiver, CRU, MIPI PHY and post-processing implementation together.

Local integration differences:
- Expose optional attributes on the I2C device, without a newer global
  Rockchip HDMI class dependency.
- Omit the external RKCIF soft-reset hook unavailable in this BSP. Bridge
  CSI recovery remains enabled. RKCIF is a separate loadable module.
- Retain Aiden's two-block digital HDMI 1080p60 EDID.
- Serialize userspace EDID updates and restart receiver training afterwards.
- Return ENOLCK for absent video instead of reporting fallback VGA timings.
- Guard optional IRQs, retain V4L2 client data, lock control updates and
  observe live AVI readiness during polling.
- Retry failed receiver training every 10 seconds without a plugin GPIO.
  SCH v1 routes Plugin_DET to the MCU; no RV1106 GPIO is invented here.

The DTS retains the onboard 24 MHz oscillator, GPIO1_A0 power enable,
active-low GPIO1_A1 reset, GPIO1_B1 IRQ and four continuous-clock CSI lanes.
No GPIO override is used for HDMI HPD.
